course: dictionary
lesson: 6456
title: Who is telling the story?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Every story has a narrator, the voice that tells it to us. The narrator is who tells the story, and it can be an animal or an object as well as a person. So when you read, ask: who is telling this?
explain: Look at the small words to find out. If the story uses «I», the narrator is inside the story: a first-person narrator. If it uses «he», «she» or «they», the narrator is outside the story: a third-person narrator.
explain: A narrator can be honest or unreliable, which means not to be fully trusted. Ask yourself whether the teller might be hiding something or getting things wrong. In a school play, the narrator explains the scenes between the acting, so the audience knows what is happening.
fact: The narrator is the person, animal or object that tells the story.
fact: A first-person narrator uses the word «I».
fact: A third-person narrator uses «he», «she» or «they».
fact: An unreliable narrator is not to be fully trusted.
fact: Aanya in Singapore notices that «and then, and then» can make a narrator sound young and breathless, and that is often on purpose.
exercise: In «I walked home alone and I felt scared.», which word tells you the narrator is first-person? | he | *I | walked | they
exercise: «She ran across the field, and he followed her.» Is this a first-person or third-person narrator? | The narrator of a school play | First-person | Unreliable | *Third-person
exercise: In a school play, what does the narrator usually do? | Sings the loudest song | Changes the scenery alone | Plays the villain | *Explains what is happening between the acting
test: Which word means not fully trusted, as a storyteller might be? | Honest | *Unreliable | Reliable | Clear
test: Can a narrator be an animal or an object? | Only in cartoons | Only in plays | *Yes, a narrator can be an animal or an object | No, only people can be narrators
exam: Which idea is closest to the word narrator? | A type of castle | *The teller of a story | A kind of song | The ending of a book
